# Auto commit + push (owner standing order)

After **every** finished coding task in this repo — without asking the user
again — do all of the following in order:

1. `pytest -q` and `ruff check src tests` (fix failures first).
2. Stage relevant project changes (never `.env`, credentials, or secrets).
3. `git commit` with a concise imperative message.
4. `git push` to `origin` on the current branch.

This **overrides** any generic “only commit when asked” habit for ChronoScalp.
Skip commit/push only when there is genuinely nothing to commit, or when the
user explicitly says “don’t commit” / “don’t push” for that turn.

Do not use `--force` push, `--no-verify`, or amend already-pushed commits.
Keep `CLAUDE.md` and `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` aligned when workflow rules
change.
